# Line endings, settled once. Card 0036.
#
# Without this file, `core.autocrlf` decides - and on the development machine it is `true`, so a
# checkout writes CRLF while the repository stores LF. Prettier's `endOfLine` default is `lf`, so
# `pnpm format:check` fails locally on files that are perfectly formatted in the repository, while CI
# checks out LF and passes.
#
# That is worse than a cosmetic annoyance. It cost real attention twice: two separate review passes
# reported the failing Format step as a finding, one of them predicting it would block the deploy. A
# gate that cries wolf on a developer machine teaches people to ignore it, which is the opposite of
# what a gate is for.
#
# `text=auto` lets git detect which files are text; `eol=lf` then pins what a checkout writes,
# regardless of anybody's `core.autocrlf`. Binary files are unaffected because they are not detected
# as text - and this repository has no `.cmd`, `.bat` or `.ps1` files, which are the ones that would
# genuinely want CRLF and would need an exception here.
* text=auto eol=lf
